# tests.list -- iSH-AOK's processor tests, as AOK VM's guests run them (cpu-image.sh builds them, run1.sh's
# cpu workload runs them, cpu-cmp.sh reads the transcripts). A line a test:
#   ARCH NAME SOURCE CHECK [FLAGS]
# ARCH: x86_64, i386 (a 32-bit program, on the x86_64 guest: their answers are a 64-bit kernel's), aarch64,
# riscv64. CHECK: S, a "NAME: PASS" line and status 0 (test_common.h's); Xn, exit status n (the assembly
# tests); D, no verdict of its own: its output against the oracle's. FLAGS: the compiler's, where not
# "-O2 -static -pthread ... -lm -ldl"; asm: an assembly test with its own _start (and its flags after).
